# song mode (CLIPS, KNOB 4: OFF, LOOP, ONE SHOT): the track plays its clips after each other, from the one it is on, while they
# have steps. The first clip without steps ends the run: LOOP starts the run again, ONE SHOT goes on to that empty clip and stays there.
# Clips are numbered from 0 here, as the tests show them: clip 0 has its starting steps, clips 1 and 2 get one step, clip 3 stays empty
tap HOME
tap PLAY
wait 300
tapkey b0
tapkey w1
waitpos 0 0
wait 100
expect clip 1
tap SEQ
tapkey w0
tap SAVE
tap SAVE
tap HOME
tapkey w2
waitpos 0 0
wait 100
expect clip 2
tap SEQ
tapkey w0
tap SAVE
tap SAVE
tap HOME
tapkey w3
waitpos 0 0
wait 100
expect clip 3
expect stepoff 0
# LOOP: the run is clips 0, 1 and 2; after clip 2 it starts again at clip 0
turn K4 1
expect song 1
tapkey w0
waitpos 0 0
wait 100
expect clip 0
expect queued 1
waitpos 0 0
wait 100
expect clip 1
expect queued 2
waitpos 0 0
wait 100
expect clip 2
expect queued 0
waitpos 0 0
wait 100
expect clip 0
expect queued 1
# ONE SHOT: from clip 0 on, the run ends on the empty clip 3, which plays nothing and stays there
turn K4 1
expect song 2
waitpos 0 0
wait 100
expect clip 1
expect queued 2
waitpos 0 0
wait 100
expect clip 2
expect queued 3
waitpos 0 0
wait 100
expect clip 3
expect queued 255
waitpos 0 0
wait 100
expect clip 3
# OFF: nothing follows the clip
turn K4 -2
expect song 0
tapkey w0
waitpos 0 0
wait 100
expect clip 0
expect queued 255
waitpos 0 0
wait 100
expect clip 0
